  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Creating Resilient Agricultural Systems for Vulnerable Communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to enhance the resilience of vulnerable mountain communities in Pakistan (Gilgit-Baltistan and Chitral) by strengthening climate-adaptive agricultural livelihoods and promoting sustainable natural resource management. Specifically, it seeks to:  

1. Increase access to diversified and sustainable agricultural livelihood opportunities, improving household food security and income stability. 

2. Promote the adoption of climate-smart and innovative solutions, including regenerative farming practices, efficient water management systems, and inclusive green business models. 

3. Empower women and youth through targeted support for women-led greenhouses, micro-grants, and green entrepreneurship, ensuring equitable participation in climate-resilient development.</narrative>
  </description>
